  "body": "The need for this change derives from the chromium bug introduced into Chrome v70+. The report for this issue is located at: https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=897373 and a stackoverflow item located here: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/52901043/chrome-v70-has-issue-with-innertext-in-td-cells\r\n\r\nThe original Chrome developer Yoshifumi Inoue (yosin@chromium.org) has requested we see if there is a consensus to change the spec from what it is now: \r\n\r\nFrom https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#inner-text-collection-steps Step 6:\r\n\r\n> If node's computed value of 'display' is 'table-cell', and node's CSS box is not the last 'table-cell' box of its enclosing 'table-row' box, then append a string containing a single U+0009 CHARACTER TABULATION (tab) character to items.\r\n\r\nThe problem is when a call to innerText on a single td cell is made, it returns a TAB character. A possible solution is to reframe this to add the TAB character only when using innerText on a table, row or the like, again not when calling innerText on a single td cell.\r\n\r\nIf there are any arguments against this change in the spec, please add your comments to this issue. Thank you!\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n",
